# The byte content of these files *is* the evidence: every one of them is pinned
# by a published SHA-256. Git must therefore never normalise their line endings.
#
# Without this file, `core.autocrlf=true` stores the working-tree CRLF as LF, so a
# fresh clone reproduces different bytes and none of the published hashes verify
# (C caught exactly this on the first delivery: the committed blobs hashed to
# 4142a248... while the published value for 600519 normalized is 75caedb8...).
*.json -text
